ser2netweb source package
=========================

The upstream tarball is the release tag's archive from GitHub, repacked by
uscan without vendor/wheels (Files-Excluded in debian/copyright), hence the
+ds suffix:

  uscan --download-current-version

ser2netweb/web/static/ holds the minified browser libraries the web UI loads
(htmx, xterm.js and its fit addon), as the npm releases ship them.
debian/missing-sources/ has their sources: htmx's unminified dist/htmx.js and
the TypeScript src/ trees of @xterm/xterm and @xterm/addon-fit.
packaging/debian/missing_sources.py (in the upstream tarball) fetches them from
the npm registry, checking each tarball against the integrity hash in
vendor/npm/package.json and the static files against those releases:

  python3 packaging/debian/missing_sources.py .

The recipe is kept upstream in packaging/debian/ of
https://github.com/haliskilic/ser2netweb, where CI builds it in Debian
unstable, Debian 13 and Ubuntu 26.04 containers and runs lintian.

